.TH TREE 1
.SH NAME
tree \- display a sorted directory tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tree
[\-ad] [\-L level] [\-\-] [directory ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List directory entries in bytewise name order using ASCII branches.
The default root is the current directory. Symbolic links show their targets
and are never recursively traversed. The final report counts displayed
subdirectories and files, including links but excluding the starting roots.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Include names beginning with a dot, except . and ...
.TP
.B \-d
Show directories only; symbolic links to directories are still links.
.TP
.B \-L level
Limit displayed levels below each root. The first level is 1.
.SH LIMITS
Paths including their terminator must fit 256 native characters.
Each directory is read and closed before descending; sorted names remain in
memory until its children have been visited. Memory and path length bound traversal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on traversal or output failure, 2 for invalid options.
